1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,015
This is me.

2
00:00:01,195 --> 00:00:02,708
On top of a pyramid.

3
00:00:02,888 --> 00:00:05,751
Wearing a crown that weighs more than my entire body.

4
00:00:05,931 --> 00:00:08,251
Below me, ten thousand people are bowing.

5
00:00:08,431 --> 00:00:09,139
To me!

6
00:00:09,319 --> 00:00:12,654
And somewhere out there, the real Pharaoh is about to find out.

7
00:00:12,834 --> 00:00:16,987
So how did a regular guy in a red cap become the king of Ancient Egypt?

8
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:18,035
Honestly?

9
00:00:18,215 --> 00:00:19,434
Total accident.

10
00:00:19,734 --> 00:00:20,860
Let me rewind.

11
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:27,650
It all started on a boring Saturday morning.

12
00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:29,421
I was cleaning my bedroom.

13
00:00:29,601 --> 00:00:32,239
Okay, I was pretending to clean my bedroom.

14
00:00:32,419 --> 00:00:36,848
And under my bed, behind a pizza box from last month, I found something weird.

15
00:00:37,248 --> 00:00:38,774
A small golden box.

16
00:00:38,954 --> 00:00:40,927
Covered in strange little pictures.

17
00:00:41,107 --> 00:00:43,553
Birds, eyes, snakes, a guy with a dog head.

18
00:00:43,733 --> 00:00:46,418
And right in the middle, one big shiny red button.

19
00:00:46,598 --> 00:00:49,726
Now, any sensible person would put it down and walk away.

20
00:00:49,906 --> 00:00:51,580
So obviously, I pressed it.

21
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:52,552
Click.

22
00:00:52,732 --> 00:00:53,359
Hum.

23
00:00:53,539 --> 00:00:54,134
Whoosh!

24
00:00:54,314 --> 00:00:58,411
My bedroom turned into a giant spinning tunnel of gold and blue light.

25
00:00:58,591 --> 00:01:02,774
My socks went one way, my comic books went the other way, and I went backwards.

26
00:01:02,954 --> 00:01:05,552
About four thousand five hundred years backwards.

27
00:01:06,052 --> 00:01:08,241
I landed face first in hot sand.

28
00:01:08,421 --> 00:01:10,440
When I looked up, I couldn't believe it.

29
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:11,446
Pyramids!

30
00:01:11,626 --> 00:01:12,551
Real ones!

31
00:01:12,731 --> 00:01:18,043
Shiny and new, covered in smooth white limestone, sparkling in the sun like giant diamonds.

32
00:01:18,223 --> 00:01:20,373
Fun fact: that's what they really looked like.

33
00:01:20,553 --> 00:01:23,021
The rough stones you see today were the inside.

34
00:01:23,521 --> 00:01:27,314
I was taking a selfie with the pyramids when I heard a noise behind me.

35
00:01:27,494 --> 00:01:28,259
Spears.

36
00:01:28,439 --> 00:01:29,590
Lots of spears.

37
00:01:29,770 --> 00:01:33,276
Two guards with very serious faces and very pointy weapons.

38
00:01:33,456 --> 00:01:35,119
I said, hi, I come in peace!

39
00:01:35,299 --> 00:01:37,397
They did not understand a single word.

40
00:01:37,577 --> 00:01:39,683
So they picked me up and carried me away.

41
00:01:39,863 --> 00:01:41,414
Like a sack of potatoes.

42
00:01:42,014 --> 00:01:44,053
They took me straight to the royal palace.

43
00:01:44,233 --> 00:01:47,646
Huge columns, painted walls, golden statues everywhere.

44
00:01:47,826 --> 00:01:48,972
And it was empty.

45
00:01:49,152 --> 00:01:50,508
The throne was empty!

46
00:01:50,688 --> 00:01:53,399
The Pharaoh had gone away on a long trip up the Nile.

47
00:01:53,899 --> 00:01:55,593
Then the royal priest saw my head.

48
00:01:55,773 --> 00:01:56,820
My red cap.

49
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,617
He gasped, pointed at the ceiling, and started yelling.

50
00:01:59,797 --> 00:02:05,445
Turns out, the ancient Egyptians had a red crown, called the Deshret, the crown of Lower Egypt.

51
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:10,874
In their eyes, a stranger falling from the sky wearing a red crown could only mean one thing.

52
00:02:11,054 --> 00:02:15,459
Within five minutes, they put me on the throne, handed me a crook and a flail, and bowed.

53
00:02:15,639 --> 00:02:16,823
I was the Pharaoh!

54
00:02:17,423 --> 00:02:19,665
And let me tell you, being Pharaoh is awesome.

55
00:02:19,845 --> 00:02:21,962
Servants fanning you with giant feathers.

56
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:22,794
Grapes.

57
00:02:22,974 --> 00:02:23,923
Honey cakes.

58
00:02:24,103 --> 00:02:26,298
A pet cat that was treated like royalty.

59
00:02:26,478 --> 00:02:31,058
The ancient Egyptians loved cats so much, they believed some cats were sacred.

60
00:02:31,558 --> 00:02:33,450
Then came my first royal meeting.

61
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:36,911
My architects rolled out the plans for a brand new pyramid.

62
00:02:37,091 --> 00:02:38,386
It was very serious.

63
00:02:38,566 --> 00:02:39,710
Very precise.

64
00:02:39,890 --> 00:02:41,094
And very boring.

65
00:02:41,274 --> 00:02:44,732
They handed me a reed pen, and asked me to approve the design.

66
00:02:44,912 --> 00:02:46,847
So I made one small improvement.

67
00:02:47,027 --> 00:02:48,198
I drew a slide.

68
00:02:48,378 --> 00:02:51,460
A giant slide, all the way down the side of the pyramid.

69
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:53,880
Here's the thing about being Pharaoh.

70
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:55,465
Nobody tells you no.

71
00:02:55,645 --> 00:02:58,723
Within a week, hundreds of workers were building my slide.

72
00:02:58,903 --> 00:03:02,353
And by the way, these workers weren't slaves, like the old movies say.

73
00:03:02,533 --> 00:03:04,486
Archaeologists found their village.

74
00:03:04,666 --> 00:03:08,739
They were skilled, paid workers who got bread, beer, and even medical care.

75
00:03:09,239 --> 00:03:10,638
Finally, the big day.

76
00:03:10,818 --> 00:03:12,438
The whole city came to watch.

77
00:03:12,618 --> 00:03:15,454
I climbed to the top, sat down, and said: here we go.

78
00:03:15,634 --> 00:03:18,612
It turns out polished limestone is extremely slippery.

79
00:03:18,792 --> 00:03:19,576
Faster.

80
00:03:19,756 --> 00:03:20,540
Faster.

81
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:21,452
FASTER!

82
00:03:21,752 --> 00:03:26,955
I flew off the end of the slide, sailed over the crowd, and landed right in a horse drawn chariot.

83
00:03:27,135 --> 00:03:28,456
The horses panicked.

84
00:03:28,636 --> 00:03:29,910
The driver screamed.

85
00:03:30,090 --> 00:03:35,388
And we went galloping across the desert, through a market, past a camel, and straight towards the river.

86
00:03:35,888 --> 00:03:37,641
We stopped at the edge of the Nile.

87
00:03:37,821 --> 00:03:39,932
And that's when I noticed something terrible.

88
00:03:40,112 --> 00:03:41,486
The river was rising.

89
00:03:41,666 --> 00:03:42,326
Fast.

90
00:03:42,506 --> 00:03:43,681
Way too fast.

91
00:03:44,081 --> 00:03:45,775
Every year, the Nile flooded.

92
00:03:45,955 --> 00:03:49,935
The Egyptians called it the inundation, and it was actually a good thing.

93
00:03:50,115 --> 00:03:53,855
The water left behind rich black mud, perfect for growing wheat.

94
00:03:54,035 --> 00:03:56,265
But this year, the flood was way too big.

95
00:03:56,445 --> 00:03:58,865
It was heading straight for the farms and the village.

96
00:03:59,045 --> 00:04:02,467
Everyone's food for the whole year was about to be washed away.

97
00:04:03,067 --> 00:04:05,538
And then, staring at the water, I had an idea.

98
00:04:05,718 --> 00:04:06,662
My slide!

99
00:04:06,842 --> 00:04:10,513
If water can slide down a pyramid, it can slide down anything.

100
00:04:10,693 --> 00:04:12,847
What if we built long slides on the ground?

101
00:04:13,027 --> 00:04:13,781
Channels!

102
00:04:13,961 --> 00:04:18,515
To carry the water away from the village, and spread it across the dry fields instead.

103
00:04:19,015 --> 00:04:21,543
As Pharaoh, I gave my first good order ever.

104
00:04:21,723 --> 00:04:22,344
Dig!

105
00:04:22,524 --> 00:04:23,596
Everybody dig!

106
00:04:23,776 --> 00:04:26,917
Farmers, workers, guards, even the priests grabbed shovels.

107
00:04:27,097 --> 00:04:34,334
We dug all night, using the same smart tools the Egyptians really used, like the shaduf, a big wooden lever for lifting water.

108
00:04:34,834 --> 00:04:37,118
At sunrise, the water reached the channels.

109
00:04:37,298 --> 00:04:38,186
It turned.

110
00:04:38,366 --> 00:04:39,233
It flowed.

111
00:04:39,413 --> 00:04:43,465
It spread out across the dry fields, and left the village completely safe.

112
00:04:43,645 --> 00:04:45,014
The crowd went wild.

113
00:04:45,194 --> 00:04:46,786
They lifted me up and cheered.

114
00:04:46,966 --> 00:04:47,834
Honestly?

115
00:04:48,014 --> 00:04:49,372
Best day of my life.

116
00:04:49,972 --> 00:04:51,869
And then the real Pharaoh came home.

117
00:04:52,049 --> 00:04:58,054
He walked into the throne room, and saw a short stranger in a red cap, sitting on his throne, eating his grapes.

118
00:04:58,234 --> 00:04:59,582
The room went silent.

119
00:04:59,762 --> 00:05:01,491
Somebody dropped a honey cake.

120
00:05:02,091 --> 00:05:03,654
I was sure this was the end.

121
00:05:03,834 --> 00:05:06,209
But then his advisers told him everything.

122
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:10,193
The slide, the chariot, the flood, and the channels that saved the farms.

123
00:05:10,373 --> 00:05:12,782
The Pharaoh looked at me for a very long time.

124
00:05:12,962 --> 00:05:14,204
And then, he smiled.

125
00:05:14,704 --> 00:05:18,508
He gave me a golden necklace, and made me Royal Inventor of Egypt.

126
00:05:18,688 --> 00:05:20,166
Then he took his crown back.

127
00:05:20,346 --> 00:05:21,416
Which was fair.

128
00:05:21,596 --> 00:05:22,742
It was his crown.

129
00:05:23,242 --> 00:05:26,374
Suddenly, the golden box in my pocket started buzzing.

130
00:05:26,554 --> 00:05:28,078
The red button was glowing.

131
00:05:28,258 --> 00:05:30,350
I waved goodbye, pressed it, and whoosh.

132
00:05:30,530 --> 00:05:32,040
I was back in my bedroom.

133
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:33,555
Same pizza box.

134
00:05:33,735 --> 00:05:35,056
Same messy floor.

135
00:05:35,236 --> 00:05:36,832
Like nothing ever happened.

136
00:05:37,332 --> 00:05:42,288
On Monday, in history class, I opened my textbook to the chapter on Ancient Egypt.

137
00:05:42,468 --> 00:05:44,835
There was a photo of a famous tomb painting.

138
00:05:45,015 --> 00:05:46,579
Workers digging channels.

139
00:05:46,759 --> 00:05:48,440
Water flowing into the fields.

140
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:53,304
And in the middle, being carried by the crowd, was a little white figure, wearing a red cap.

141
00:05:54,104 --> 00:05:57,266
If you enjoyed my disaster, subscribe to History World!

142
00:05:57,446 --> 00:06:01,225
Because next time, I might accidentally invent pizza in Ancient Rome!
